inline.s:
In the mountain of the five aggregates, the ground of stillness and cessation;
the six windows stand open and empty, and light is born in the night.
You need only wake the master within the hut;
let him not cover and bury himself in dullness.

From Nanyue and Caoxi one vein descends;
the transmission says the bright mirror is no stand either.
The diamond eye of true seeing is shared by all;
it must be opened by that one phrase about grinding a brick.

The great matter of birth and death admits no bargaining;
to speak of it breaks the heart and severs the entrails.
Through countless kalpas we have let it slip by;
this time, how could we bear to fail the King of Emptiness?

The ocean assembly of the ten directions is my home;
in coming and going, the road I pass is never wrong.
Fragrant rice eaten to the full, I turn my head and go;
beyond the gate the misty waters stretch still farther without bound.

Gazing south from the hundred cities, all is misty waves;
to meet at a peak’s summit — what would that be like?
It is not that Sudhana lacked a face;
it is only that the teacher’s faith had gone astray.

Meeting beneath the tree was an old affinity;
since we parted, I have not counted how many lives ago.
Entering the gate, one smile, and the minds met;
only then did I believe that wordlessness is the secret transmission.

In the market, one room as cold as ice;
sitting cross-legged beneath the long-burning midnight lamp.
The Arhats come and go, and the seats are always full;
everyone knows that this is a monk who stays at home.
